1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:10,600
The chart shows the instrument you picked in your watchlist.

2
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:16,500
Each candle is one slice of time. Green means the price went up.

3
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:22,100
Prices run down the right-hand side.

4
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:28,400
Time runs along the bottom.

5
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:34,100
Click the timeframe button to change how long each candle covers.

6
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:44,500
5m means every candle is five minutes.

7
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:50,700
1h gives you a wider view — one candle per hour.

8
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:56,300
These buttons along the bottom set how far back you look.

9
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:02,600
5D shows the last five days.

10
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:08,600
1M shows the last month.

11
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:14,600
1D brings you back to today.

